<p>Thanks for the feedback.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">response</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>You don't need to apologize about criticism, I'm pretty aware that dialogue isn't my strong suit. I have a sort of comfort zone when writing characters, and the D-Class &amp; Captain were pretty far outside of it, so it felt sort of weak.</p>
<p>Beyond that, the grammatical stuff (using wrong words) mostly seems to come from the fact that I really never got enough criticism on this sort of writing from people experienced with it, since I always shy away from posting. I'll probably need to look a little closer at that on my next attempt.</p>
<p>Capitalization was a bit erratic, it's a stupid habit of mine I've been trying to break for years.</p>
<p>I guess for the whole [REDACTED] thing, it felt like it was an entity/anomaly that wasn't supposed to be defined by it's appearance. I get it, it's lazy writing, but I dunno. I have a crystal clear image of what they're supposed to look like (written down on a google doc with my other stuff), so it's not a cop-out at least. For the antisocial/sociopathic section, it was definitely more of a plot device. Antisocial was so I had a way to contain the entity without much risk of a reactive event, and sociopathic for the D-17729 log/last collapsible. It's not the best, but I'm not sure how to circumvent that.</p>
<p>Destruction of all memories was a bit unnecessary, but now it's kind of integral for the exploration log, and I can't quite figure out how to get rid of it without the exploration log falling apart. I always saw entities that destroy memories as a sort of self-preservation tactic to avoid being caught/detected. But it's definitely a bit of a throwaway, and in retrospect a couple of ideas like that seem to crop up in the piece.</p>
<p>The last addendum was a pure stream-of-consciousness, but I think that it might need a little work. I just don't know what would be best to change about it for the sake of impact without accidentally ruining it's tempo.</p>
<p>Thanks a bunch for the criticisms. I'm not sure how much I'm gonna tear up in the article yet (I tried to change the basic errors, but I'm pondering how I could amend the D-17729 section's prose.) but I'll try.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

