<p>This isn't too bad, though I feel it suffers from a few similarities to other contest entries. I'm not sure the ending had much of an effect, and I'm sort of lost as to the precise origin, though it seems the Foundation is, too, so that's maybe not so bad. (I mean, I've never felt someone watching me in my life; I always assumed that was just literary convenience, like love at first sight.) Couple things:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Often times those who experience SCP-3000 tend to report it from ‘behind’. If their back is to the wall, wherever the nearest window or darkest corner in their sight is, they tend to avoid.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Doesn't make sense as worded.</p>
