<p>I had a more specific comment lined up, but Buttfranklin basically covered most of my points first, so eh.</p>
<p>I will say that this has a bunch of different effects, some of which (like the memory thing and it messing with space) seem to be there without rhyme or reason. I like the idea of something erasing people to cover its tracks, but there's very little indication of that in the article (then again, I suppose it'd be difficult for the Foundation to work that out).</p>
<p>Also, I'm not really sure how much the second log works at all. To me, at least, it doesn't do anything that a reader couldn't infer from the first addendum, and whilst that's not necessarily a killer, the dodgy dialogue hampers its creepiness.</p>
<p>There's also a couple of stylistic things; the &quot;zero (0)&quot; stuff is kinda pointless, and I feel like 'his' and the like in the containment procedures should be gender-neutral. On the other hand, the &quot;eyes in the back of their mouth&quot; is a really good line, and form some reason I like the idea of something necessitating a house 'set' to be built to contain it. There's good stuff in here, and you've structured and paced it well, it just doesn't really do it for me, I'm afraid.</p>
