<p>For the ending, I think it was definitely an open to interpretation thing. I initally thought it to be a sort of &quot;if the d-class on the other end said goodbye, what's trying to make edits&quot; thing, and you're the one that locks it (since I had no real way to allow you to input Y/N to my knowledge), but the idea that the editor PC is being locked by the entity is another way to look at it.</p>
