<p>I liked a lot of this. The containment procedures being trapping someone in a haunted house was very neat.</p>
<p>I actually like the dictionary definition thing. One important thing to note from a psychology standpoint, <a href="https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antisocial_personality_disorder">antisocial personality disorder</a> <strong>IS</strong> sociopathy. If you're looking for people who avoid social contact, that's <a href="https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avoidant_personality_disorder">avoidant personality disorder</a>.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">The real weakest part was the MTF exploration log. The dialogue with a couple of people disappearing was ok, and it's definitely interesting that they're immediately exploring a ruined site, but it really mostly just rehashed what happens in just about every MTF exploration log.</span> Edit: Actually, you know, it's fine.</p>
<p>Other than that, all the DATA EXPUNGED violence is pretty cliche, as is it erasing people. I like the whole &quot;murder after three times&quot; thing because it really tied this back into making ghost stories/superstitions true thing. I just think it would be way more interesting to give a real answer that had some thought about the beings rather than &quot;EXPUNGED carved bones EXPUNGED.&quot;</p>

