			<div class="content" id="post-content-2792483">
									

<p>I know we're talking edits for after the contest here, but yeah, it's still (as of edit 31) kinda iffy.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Think about it this way: the violence works on two levels. There's the weird/unexpected/gross factor, and then there's the fact that it serves to communicate info about these critters. We can infer from the rest of the article that they follow you but don't like being noticed, or noticing them breaks a &quot;rule,&quot; and the sheer violence of their response supports that. The fact that the procedure is so perfectly described and uniform (exactly 117.2 sec, they always do the skin thing etc) suggests that either they are creatures of unchanging habit or inflexible rule-following, or that their response is a ritual intended to accomplish a specific task or send a specific message. The bone-carving and shaping remains into a pattern support these ideas.</p>
<p>So on the information end, what are they trying to accomplish? All I've got is that maybe the bone carving and such is a ritual that results in the erasure. I only got that idea just now, like 5 days later, so it's not exactly front and center. That, or this is just &quot;what they do.&quot;</p>
<p>On the gross-out/weird end, [DATA EXPUNGED] and [REDACTED] (when used well) are generally placed so that the reader already had a good idea of what's in the box, but leaving them to work out the horrific details. You're already saying the gross stuff out loud, so the expungements aren't doing you much good.</p>
<p>So, basically, it's not hitting either purpose hard enough. I'm not saying you need to 100% spell out the motivations of the beings (you shouldn't) or that there's a particular way I think you should use your redactions. I'm just saying pick your reveals and concealments in this section to maximize both of those factors.</p>
</div>
</div>
